    <h3>What to Know Before You Buy</h3>
    <ul class="consider-list">
      <li><b>Visual comfort &amp; glare</b> — minimize direct glare, especially near desks and screens.</li>
      <li><b>Ceiling type</b> — confirm suspended/drop grid vs. drywall before choosing a mounting style.</li>
      <li><b>Ceiling-grid dimensions</b> — verify actual grid size (2×2 vs. 2×4) before ordering panels.</li>
      <li><b>Existing infrastructure</b> — note whether you're retrofitting fluorescent troffers or starting fresh.</li>
      <li><b>Light distribution</b> — even spread across desks and walkways reduces eye strain.</li>
      <li><b>CCT</b> — most offices land between 3500K–4000K for alertness without harshness.</li>
      <li><b>CRI</b> — 80+ is typical for accurate color rendering in workspaces.</li>
      <li><b>Dimming &amp; controls</b> — confirm compatibility with 0-10V dimming or occupancy sensors.</li>
      <li><b>Voltage compatibility</b> — confirm building voltage (120V, 277V, or universal) before ordering.</li>
      <li><b>Installation method</b> — recessed, surface-mount, or grid-mount changes which fixture fits.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Choosing the Right Light</h3>
    <div class="fixture-grid">
      <article class="fixture-card">
        <span class="fixture-card__name">Panel Lights</span>
        <p class="fixture-card__best">Best for <strong>suspended / drop-ceiling offices</strong> that need clean, uniform illumination with low glare.</p>
        <ul class="fixture-card__points">
          <li>Confirm grid size (2×2 or 2×4) before ordering</li>
          <li>Diffused optics reduce screen glare</li>
          <li>Pairs well with 0-10V dimming systems</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="fixture-card__cta" href="https://www.nuwattlighting.com/collections/led-panel-light">Shop Panel Lights →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="fixture-card">
        <span class="fixture-card__name">Tube Lights</span>
        <p class="fixture-card__best">Best for offices with <strong>existing linear fluorescent troffers</strong> being retrofitted rather than replaced.</p>
        <ul class="fixture-card__points">
          <li>Verify ballast type: plug-and-play vs. ballast bypass</li>
          <li>Matches existing 4ft/2ft fixture housings</li>
          <li>Lower disruption than a full fixture swap</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="fixture-card__cta" href="https://www.nuwattlighting.com/collections/led-tube-lights">Shop Tube Lights →</a>
      </article>
