      <li><b>Ceiling design</b> — architectural or drop ceilings each favor different fixture types.</li>
      <li><b>Color rendering</b> — accurate CRI supports a polished, professional appearance.</li>
      <li><b>Circulation vs. seating</b> — different zones can call for different fixture styles.</li>
      <li><b>Dimming/controls</b> — useful for shifting mood between business hours and after-hours use.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Choosing the Right Light</h3>
    <div class="fixture-grid">
      <article class="fixture-card">
        <span class="fixture-card__name">Recessed Lights</span>
        <p class="fixture-card__best">More <strong>architectural, controlled lighting</strong> — best for accent zones, seating nooks, and design-forward areas.</p>
        <ul class="fixture-card__points">
          <li>Built-in, low-profile appearance</li>
          <li>Good for highlighting seating or reception features</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="fixture-card__cta" href="https://www.nuwattlighting.com/collections/recessed-lighting">Shop Recessed Lights →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="fixture-card">
        <span class="fixture-card__name">Panel Lights</span>
        <p class="fixture-card__best"><strong>Broad, uniform general illumination</strong> — best for larger circulation and waiting areas with a drop ceiling.</p>
        <ul class="fixture-card__points">
          <li>Even coverage for larger open lobbies</li>
          <li>Grid-mount for suspended ceilings</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="fixture-card__cta" href="https://www.nuwattlighting.com/collections/led-panel-light">Shop Panel Lights →</a>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h3>Avoidable Buying Mistakes</h3>
    <div class="mistake-box">
      <ul>
        <li>Using one fixture type uniformly across zones with different needs</li>
        <li>Ignoring glare in seating sightlines</li>
        <li>Mismatched CCT between adjoining spaces (lobby vs. hallway)</li>
        <li>Skipping dimming/control options in guest-facing lobbies</li>
        <li>Overlooking ceiling type when selecting mounting method</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>Before You Order</h3>
    <div class="checklist">
      <span class="checklist__title">Lobbies &amp; Waiting Areas — Pre-Order Checklist</span>
      <ul>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Zones identified (circulation vs. seating vs. accent)</label></li>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Fixture type matched to zone (recessed vs. panel)</label></li>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> CCT/CRI consistent with adjoining spaces</label></li>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Dimming/control compatibility confirmed</label></li>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Ceiling type and mounting method confirmed</label></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <a class="back-to-apps" href="#choose-application">↑ Back to Applications</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= OUTDOOR ================= -->
<section class="app-section" id="outdoor">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="app-section__head">
      <span class="app-section__num">Application 07 / 07</span>
      <h2>Outdoor Lighting</h2>
      <p class="app-section__intro">Outdoor fixtures live or die on environmental fit. Mounting location, wet-rating, and beam distribution matter more here than anywhere else in this guide — an indoor-rated fixture is never the right answer outside.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="quick-select">
      <div class="quick-select__label">
        <span class="tag">Quick Selection</span>
        <span class="best-for">Flood + Bullet + Wall Pack + Canopy</span>
      </div>
      <div class="quick-select__body">
        <div class="quick-select__row"><span class="k">Prioritize</span><span class="v">Environmental/wet rating, mounting location &amp; height, beam distribution, glare/light trespass, controls</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>What to Know Before You Buy</h3>
    <ul class="consider-list">
      <li><b>Wet/weather exposure</b> — every outdoor fixture should carry a wet-location rating fit for its mounting location.</li>
      <li><b>Mounting location &amp; height</b> — pole, wall, or ceiling mount changes beam spread and coverage.</li>
      <li><b>Beam/distribution</b> — broad flood patterns suit open areas; directional patterns suit accent or security use.</li>
      <li><b>Security</b> — coverage and output should match the safety needs of the area (entries, lots, perimeters).</li>
      <li><b>Light trespass &amp; glare</b> — minimize spill onto neighboring properties or public ways.</li>
      <li><b>Operating hours</b> — photocell or timed controls reduce energy use during daylight.</li>
      <li><b>Controls</b> — dusk-to-dawn sensors and motion controls are standard for most outdoor applications.</li>
      <li><b>Corrosion/environmental exposure</b> — coastal or high-moisture sites benefit from corrosion-resistant housings.</li>
      <li><b>Electrical compatibility</b> — confirm voltage and whether fixtures are hardwired, knuckle-mount, or junction-box compatible.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="ref-note">Before ordering an outdoor fixture, verify the required environmental rating and applicable project requirements. See the <a href="#professional-reference">Professional Lighting Selection &amp; Compliance Reference</a>.</p>

    <h3>Choosing the Right Light</h3>
    <div class="fixture-grid cols-4">
      <article class="fixture-card">
        <span class="fixture-card__name">Flood Lights</span>
        <p class="fixture-card__best"><strong>Broad-area illumination</strong> for lots, yards, and security applications.</p>
        <a class="fixture-card__cta" href="https://www.nuwattlighting.com/collections/led-flood-lights">Shop Flood Lights →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="fixture-card">
        <span class="fixture-card__name">Bullet Lights</span>
        <p class="fixture-card__best"><strong>Directional, spot-oriented</strong> illumination for accent and targeted security lighting.</p>
        <a class="fixture-card__cta" href="https://www.nuwattlighting.com/collections/bullet-lights">Shop Bullet Lights →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="fixture-card">
        <span class="fixture-card__name">Wall Packs</span>
        <p class="fixture-card__best"><strong>Building-mounted</strong> perimeter and entry security lighting.</p>
        <a class="fixture-card__cta" href="https://www.nuwattlighting.com/collections/led-wall-packs">Shop Wall Packs →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="fixture-card">
        <span class="fixture-card__name">Canopy Lights</span>
        <p class="fixture-card__best"><strong>Overhead lighting</strong> for covered parking, carports, and similar covered areas.</p>
        <a class="fixture-card__cta" href="https://www.nuwattlighting.com/collections/canopy-lights">Shop Canopy Lights →</a>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h3>Avoidable Buying Mistakes</h3>
    <div class="mistake-box">
      <ul>
        <li>Using indoor-rated fixtures in outdoor locations</li>
        <li>Ignoring wet-location requirements for the specific mounting location</li>
        <li>Choosing the wrong beam pattern for the area's shape and use</li>
        <li>Creating excessive glare or light trespass onto neighboring areas</li>
        <li>Overlooking environmental exposure such as corrosion or temperature extremes</li>
        <li>Skipping dusk-to-dawn or motion controls where they'd reduce operating cost</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>Before You Order</h3>
    <div class="checklist">
      <span class="checklist__title">Outdoor — Pre-Order Checklist</span>
      <ul>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Wet/damp location rating confirmed for mounting location</label></li>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Mounting height and method confirmed</label></li>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Beam pattern matched to area shape and purpose</label></li>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Light trespass/glare considered for neighboring properties</label></li>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Controls selected (photocell, motion, or timer)</label></li>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Corrosion resistance confirmed for the environment</label></li>
        <li><label><input type="checkbox"> Voltage and wiring method confirmed</label></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <a class="back-to-apps" href="#choose-application">↑ Back to Applications</a>
  </div>
</section>

